{{!< default}}

{{#post}}
<header class="about-profile outer">
    <div class="inner about-profile-inner">
        <img class="about-profile-avatar" src="{{asset "images/wordman-avatar.svg"}}" alt="Jan-Niklas Wortmann">
        <div class="about-profile-copy">
            <p class="about-profile-kicker">AI Developer Advocate &middot; JetBrains</p>
            <h1>Hey, I&apos;m Jan-Niklas</h1>
            <p>I test AI coding workflows against real codebases, then explain what held up, what broke, and why it matters for the developer shipping the result.</p>
            <div class="about-profile-links">
                <a href="{{@site.url}}/blog/">Read blog</a>
                <a href="{{@site.url}}/podcast/">Watch podcast</a>
                <a href="{{@site.url}}/calendar/">Coffee chat</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</header>

<main id="site-main" class="site-main">
    <article class="article about-page {{post_class}}">
        <section class="about-content gh-canvas">
            {{#if content}}
                {{content}}
            {{else}}
                <h2>What I Test</h2>
                <p>I work as an <strong>AI Developer Advocate at JetBrains</strong>. I test coding agents, IDE workflows, and developer-tooling ideas against the standard that matters: would I trust this in a real codebase?</p>

                <p>I&apos;m a <strong>former RxJS core team member</strong> and an <strong>Angular Google Developer Expert (GDE)</strong>. That background keeps me focused on architecture, debugging, and maintainability rather than demo magic.</p>

                <p>My take on AI tools is simple: show the workflow, show the failure modes, and make the verdict useful to developers who still own the result.</p>

                <h2>What You&apos;ll Find Here</h2>
                <p>This site is built for working web developers. I publish tested AI workflows, lessons in engineering craft, grounded takes on industry shifts, conference talks, and podcast conversations about ideas that survive contact with real code.</p>

                <h2>Outside the Experiments</h2>
                <p>When I&apos;m not testing workflows or recording conversations, I&apos;m usually chasing better coffee and spending time with my family.</p>
                <p><a href="/calendar/">Grab a coffee chat</a> if you want to swap notes on AI tools, frontend engineering, or an interesting idea.</p>
            {{/if}}
        </section>

        {{#if @custom.speaking_highlights}}
            <section class="about-highlights gh-canvas">
                <h2>Selected stages</h2>
                <div class="about-highlights-content">
                    {{{@custom.speaking_highlights}}}
                </div>
            </section>
        {{/if}}

    </article>
</main>
{{/post}}
